<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Majd al-Dawla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/997">997</a>–1029</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Majd al-Dawla was the Buyid ruler of Ray from 997 to 1029, succeeding his father Fakhr al-Dawla as a child. For many years real power was held by his mother, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayyida-shirin">Sayyida Shirin</a>, who kept the Ghaznavids at bay. After her death in 1028 he could not defend his realm, and in 1029 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> took Ray, deposed him and sent him as a prisoner to Ghazna.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/majd-al-dawla.jpg" alt="Majd al-Dawla" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_dinar_of_Majd_al-Dawla,_the_last_ruler_of_the_Buyid_amirate_of_Ray.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
